{
  "id": "COMPOUND:39573 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Linderoxide is implicated in the activation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular interactions involving SK-OV-3 cells. The evidence suggests that Linderoxide acts as a target for SK-OV-3, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Thebaine and Nocapyrone G. These compounds all ultimately lead to the activation of Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a shared mechanism of action in the context of the dataset. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Phosphodiesterase 6C in the biological response to these compounds, possibly through the modulation of intracellular signaling pathways. The presence of multiple compounds targeting SK-OV-3 and their subsequent effect on Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a broader pharmacological profile, where the activation of this enzyme may be a critical downstream event in the signaling cascade.",
